          "text": "Description: The observation of two yellow-orange orbs for several minutes, on a weekend night (at 22:45), strongly suggests Thai lanterns, likely released nearby after a private party. The observed movement is very slight (witnesses in a car, coming from the South), which is consistent with the light south wind recorded in Montauban: weather. The GEIPAN classifies this case as \"B\", probable observation of a Thai lantern. At the same time, a similar observation occurred in BRUGUIERES (31). It may be from the same origin.",
